#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:13
#: 3f776fd975ae413ba05782c15117706e
msgid "APM 2.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:17
#: 1512a1abebd24193ba7ecafebe4cfb8b
msgid "The APM 2.5 board requires no assembly, and is ready for firmware. You have a choice of side or top entry pin configuration, in order to accommodate a variety of installations. You'll see this option when you order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:25
#: 35db3bbdfe8c4accb629f346a7938e04
msgid "This page gives you a look under the hood, and goes into more detail about the design of this board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:28
#: 9cd8ad652c604ddda5eff05eefd9224f
msgid "The APM 2.5 has some improvements over the APM 2.0, but they both have a very similar layout and function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:32
#: d3da34a5c8ea4451a96295502481392d
msgid "APM 2.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:34
#: 23f354bfb74e4477919a789d56281142
msgid "**APM 2.6** is a revision of the APM that makes use of an external compass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:36
#: 6fd0f1a3010843529bde27b0970f8723
msgid "The APM 2.6 has no on board compass, and is optimized for vehicles where the compass should be placed as far from power and motor sources as possible to avoid magnetic interference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:39
#: 49cf98b0b81f40d7b99ca6072797663f
msgid "APM 2.6 is designed to be used with the 3DR GPS uBlox LEA-6 with Compass module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:41
#: 1ae1829b1eb740288ae5871bb8ba255a
msgid "The GPS/Compass module may be mounted further from noise sources than the APM itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:43
#: 53af9504be3a4812870bd4a6724b3d88
msgid "APM 2.6 requires a GPS unit with an on board compass for full autonomy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:45
#: c786e5135d704fc98db1c0d34eef9696
msgid "For information on installing a 3DR GPS uBlox LEA-6 with Compass, visit :ref:`3DR Power Module <common-installing-3dr-ublox-gps-compass-module>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:52
#: 6875cccdd4564a16ab118e2961dc7ee3
msgid "Using the APM 2.5/2.6 Enclosure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:54
#: 771debfe69404e1687928aa385a6945f
msgid "The APM 2.5/2.6 board is shipped in an enclosure with foam protecting the barometric pressure sensor, as shown here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:61
#: 87563d042dee466b835e1a89a15602ba
msgid "Not using the APM Enclosure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:63
#: b5941373f9654665967b1e72bf81a33e
msgid "If you aren't using the enclosure, make sure to cover the barometric sensor with some open cell foam, cotton padding or tissue to protect it from prop wash, wind and turbulence. Also, the barometric sensor is sensitive to light and readings can change by several meters from direct sunlight to shade. Some type of light shield (on top of the foam) will minimize the effects of light changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:78
#: 43631f2414e44c2c8422abd9fdff4a3a
msgid "The most common way to power the APM2 is to use the :ref:`3DR Power Module <common-3dr-power-module>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:80
#: 2819520bac714e218b9654eac7d2c543
msgid "Detailed information on powering the APM and providing power to Servos is provided in :ref:`Powering the APM2 <common-powering-the-apm2>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:86
#: 936ed91281c9451b9aee7548bd83c348
msgid "Explanation of solder jumper options on the bottom of the board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:92
#: 2519551eabe14914a8859825ffb35ab4
msgid "Changing your telemetry to use UART2 (aka Serial3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:94
#: 83e4bc9b9b334b579d33dfd96aa19683
msgid "By default an Xbee connected to the APM2 will use UART0 (aka \"Serial\" in Arduino) which is shared with the USB as mentioned above. If you wish to instead use UART2 (aka \"Serial3\") for telemetry you can change the \"AutoMUX UART0\" jumper on the bottom of the APM2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-apm25-and-26-overview.rst:99
#: 24a9aca6c3f94a68955238674097113b
msgid "Although difficult to see, by default there are two small jumpers between the upper pads that must be cut with an X-Acto blade. Then a new solder bridge must be made to join the bottom pads."
msgstr ""

